# AGENT.md — src/

Application root.

## What lives here

- `main.ts` — starts the server{{#if hasOrm}} and initializes the ORM connection{{/if}}. Nothing else.
- `server.ts` — builds the Hapi server (initServer factory), registers plugins
  and routes. Import this directly in tests to drive requests with
  `server.inject()` instead of starting a real server.
- `config/` — environment loading.
- `plugins/` — Hapi plugin registrations (swagger{{#if useAuth}}, auth{{/if}}).
- `errors/` — AppError base class and subclasses (NotFoundError, ValidationError).
- `shared/` — cross-cutting infrastructure (database, cache{{#if useAuth}}, auth{{/if}}{{#if useHealthCheck}}, health{{/if}}) used by more
  than one module.
- `routes/` — one directory per feature module.

## Rules

- Do not put business logic in `main.ts` or `server.ts`.
- When you add a new module, register its routes in `server.ts` with
  `server.route(moduleRoutes)` in the same change — unregistered routes
  are unreachable and fail silently.
- Plugins (swagger, auth) are registered in `server.ts` via
  `await server.register([...])`.
- Cross-cutting concerns (error formatting) use `server.ext('onPreResponse', ...)`.
{{#if useAuth}}
- Auth is set up as a JWT strategy in `plugins/auth.ts`. Apply it to a
  route by setting `options: { auth: 'jwt' }` in the route config.
{{/if}}
